Run from WSL after rebuilding and staging libsyn68k:

  bash executor/tests/run-browser-compat-tests.sh

The test executes the corrected Greg's Browser 2.7 bookmark scan using the
real 68K interpreter and a native callback. About, Preferences and Browser
Docs fixtures must skip the updater; both dialog-kind Browser and document
fixtures must receive the original window data and selector. The original
null-refCon guard and C caller's stack must survive the patch. The test also
checks version matching and repeat application.

Manual Windows verification: launch Apps/Browser, dismiss About, browse
folders, open Preferences, and use the icon menu after Special. The icon
title must be drawn as an icon suite, with no handle bytes shown as text.
Inspect stderr.txt for win_exception and pointer-mapping exhaustion.

List Manager click-loop regression:

  bash executor/tests/run-list-click-tests.sh

This runs the real LClick selection loop with controlled callback results.
A true result must select the clicked cell and reach mouse-up polling; a
false result must cancel before selection. A list without a callback must
also select normally. QuickDraw painting and mouse-up delivery are mocked.
